      "reasoning": "I see that only the activation of Fabled Passage is available — no spells are listed for casting, even though I have enough mana to cast Surrak, the Hunt Caller ({2}{G}).\n\
\n\
Since I cannot cast spells at this moment (the system does not offer them), I should either pass priority or activate an ability.\n\
\n\
Activating Fabled Passage now won't help me cast Surrak — it only searches for a basic land and requires sacrificing the Passage, which doesn't add immediate mana.\n\
\n\
Moreover, there's a spell on the stack (Kaito, Bane of Nightmares) that I might want to interact with. Since I have no counterspells or instant-speed interaction in hand, I cannot stop it.\n\
\n\
Therefore, the best play is to do nothing and let Kaito resolve.\n\
\n\
I will pass priority.\n\
\n\
